IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa24-identity`

-- coa24-tests-identity.l4: tests for ss 1110A to 1110D (coa24-identity.l4). Expected values were decided from the text
-- before the run. Penalty values are built field by field from the words of s 1110B(4).

§ `Tests for s 1110A(1)`

-- (a) verified by the registrar, no statement, not since ceased: verified.
#ASSERT `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) a verification statement delivered, not since ceased: verified.
#ASSERT `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Since ceased by virtue of regulations under (6): not verified.
#ASSERT `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Whether the regulations ended it is not in the sources: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Neither (a) nor (b): not verified, whatever the regulations.
#ASSERT `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests for s 1110A(2), (3), (5) and (9)`

#ASSERT `s 1110A(2) the statement is a verification statement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110A(2) the statement is a verification statement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1110A(2) the statement is a verification statement` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1110A(2) the statement is a verification statement` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 1110A(3) the verification statement meets the requirement to specify the supervisory authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110A(3) the verification statement meets the requirement to specify the supervisory authority` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 1110A(5) the statement may be delivered at the same time as the verification statement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110A(5) the statement may be delivered at the same time as the verification statement` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 1110A(9) the Money Laundering Regulations` EQUALS "the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692)"
#ASSERT `s 1110A(9) the authority is a supervisory authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110A(9) the authority is a supervisory authority` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests for s 1110B(4)`

-- (a) on conviction on indictment: imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both).
#ASSERT `s 1110B(4) the punishment the regulations must provide for an offence` `on conviction on indictment` NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 2, Years), `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
-- (b)(i) England and Wales: the general limit in a magistrates' court (a test figure of 6 months here) or a fine (or both).
#ASSERT `s 1110B(4) the punishment the regulations must provide for an offence` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` (JUST (Period OF 6, Months)) EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 6, Months), `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
-- The general limit is not in the Act: not covered when it is not supplied.
#ASSERT `s 1110B(4) the punishment the regulations must provide for an offence` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(ii) Scotland: 12 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both), daily default fine one-fifth of the statutory maximum.
#ASSERT `s 1110B(4) the punishment the regulations must provide for an offence` `on summary conviction in Scotland` NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 12, Months), `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 0.2), `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
-- (b)(iii) Northern Ireland: 6 months, same fine, same daily default fine.
#ASSERT `s 1110B(4) the punishment the regulations must provide for an offence` `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 6, Months), `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 0.2), `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
-- Summary conviction with no place named: paragraph (b) divides it by place, so not covered.
#ASSERT `s 1110B(4) the punishment the regulations must provide for an offence` `on summary conviction` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for s 1110C`

#ASSERT `s 1110C(1) the Secretary of State may give the notice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(1) the Secretary of State may give the notice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(1) the Secretary of State may give the notice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1110C(1) the Secretary of State may give the notice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep (fork F21): the function is named for a grant or a power ("The Secretary of State may ... if satisfied"), its gate is "if", and a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, not the text's own no; the other reading, JUST FALSE, is in the fork register
#ASSERT `s 1110C(1) the Secretary of State may give the notice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 1110C(2) the effect applies in relation to the person` `s 1110C(2)(a) section 12(2A) does not require a statement for the person named as a director` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(2) the effect applies in relation to the person` `s 1110C(2)(f) section 1098B(2)(c) does not apply in relation to the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(2) the effect applies in relation to the person` `s 1110C(2)(c) section 167M does not apply in relation to the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1110C(2) the effect applies in relation to the person` `s 1110C(2)(e) section 1067A does not apply to the delivery of documents by the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 1110C(2) the provision the effect concerns` `s 1110C(2)(a) section 12(2A) does not require a statement for the person named as a director` EQUALS "section 12(2A)"
#ASSERT `s 1110C(2) the provision the effect concerns` `s 1110C(2)(b) section 167G(3)(c) does not apply to the notice of the person having become a director` EQUALS "section 167G(3)(c)"
#ASSERT `s 1110C(2) the provision the effect concerns` `s 1110C(2)(c) section 167M does not apply in relation to the person` EQUALS "section 167M"
#ASSERT `s 1110C(2) the provision the effect concerns` `s 1110C(2)(d) section 167N(1) does not apply in relation to the person` EQUALS "section 167N(1)"
#ASSERT `s 1110C(2) the provision the effect concerns` `s 1110C(2)(e) section 1067A does not apply to the delivery of documents by the person` EQUALS "section 1067A"
#ASSERT `s 1110C(2) the provision the effect concerns` `s 1110C(2)(f) section 1098B(2)(c) does not apply in relation to the person` EQUALS "section 1098B(2)(c)"

-- (3)(a) "crime" means conduct which constitutes an offence, or is or corresponds to conduct which would in any one part.
#ASSERT `s 1110C(3)(a) the conduct is crime` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(3)(a) the conduct is crime` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(3)(a) the conduct is crime` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (3)(b) "serious": a maximum sentence of 3 years or more, or violence, substantial financial gain, or a large number of persons.
#ASSERT `s 1110C(3)(b) the crime is serious` 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(3)(b) the crime is serious` 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(3)(b) the crime is serious` 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(3)(b) the crime is serious` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(3)(b) the crime is serious` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(3)(b) the crime is serious` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110C(3)(b) the crime is serious` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests for s 1110D`

#ASSERT `s 1110D(1) the person is a relevant person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110D(1) the person is a relevant person` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (5)(a) on indictment: not more than 2 years (24 months). (5)(b) on summary conviction: not more than 3 months.
#ASSERT `s 1110D(5) the regulations may provide for imprisonment of this term` `on conviction on indictment` 24 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1110D(5) the regulations may provide for imprisonment of this term` `on conviction on indictment` 25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1110D(5) the regulations may provide for imprisonment of this term` `on summary conviction` 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1110D(5) the regulations may provide for imprisonment of this term` `on summary conviction` 4 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1110D(5) the regulations may provide for imprisonment of this term` `on summary conviction in Scotland` 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1110D(5) the regulations may provide for imprisonment of this term` `on summary conviction in Scotland` 4 EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 1110D(6) the person is a customer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1110D(6) the person is a customer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1110D(6) the person is a customer` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1110D(6) the person is a customer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
